## Reviewer reading used in PLAN_REVIEW-01

- Display y 0..192 (window controls, group title, 相簿/記事本 tab text band) is bit-exact across all
  three adjacent historical transitions, including the scan-003 frame that carries the 相溥 OCR
  misread. The selected-indicator/underline rows sit at the y 192..200 boundary and were not claimed
  as bit-exact by this probe.
- First small diffs (max channel delta <=14) appear at y 192..200; large content diffs follow below,
  consistent with scrolling content and its JPEG block coupling at the content-adjacent boundary.
- initial.png == frame-000.png == scan-000.png byte-identical (sha256 da605c7d71557e1cade2c15d74e8c697f4d8970b0940508c154c23bea2c36c42):
  unchanged screens re-capture byte-identically on this binding, so exact-equality continuity is
  operationally plausible when the frozen guard region is defined inside the stable band and the
  initialization freezes the shadow/separator exclusion zone per the plan.
